<article class="env-lemma" id="00NS">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00NS">Lemma <span data-tag="00NS">10.106.5</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a Noetherian local ring. Let $x \in \mathfrak m$. Let $M$ be a finite $R$-module such that $x$ is a nonzerodivisor on $M$ and $M/xM$ is free over $R/xR$. Then $M$ is free over $R$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $m_1, \ldots , m_ r$ be elements of $M$ which map to a $R/xR$-basis of $M/xM$. By Nakayama's Lemma <a href="/tag/00DV" data-tag="00DV">10.20.1</a> $m_1, \ldots , m_ r$ generate $M$. If $\sum a_ i m_ i = 0$ is a relation, then $a_ i \in xR$ for all $i$. Hence $a_ i = b_ i x$ for some $b_ i \in R$. Hence the kernel $K$ of $R^ r \to M$ satisfies $xK = K$ and hence is zero by Nakayama's lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>